# Shell scripts must use LF line endings.
# With Git's typical `core.autocrlf=true` setting on Windows, checkout would convert `.sh` files to CRLF.
# Bash would then read `set -euo pipefail` as `pipefail\r` and report an invalid option.
# `eol=lf` keeps these files on LF regardless of `autocrlf` across all build machines.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Build archives must not carry local signing or object-storage credentials.
certs/** export-ignore
